 ['E','Storage is not the only route to flexibility. Some consumers can shift demand, running a water heater when renewable output is abundant rather than at the evening peak. Better connections between regions can also share variations in supply. Planners therefore compare portfolios of measures rather than searching for a universally best machine. Environmental impacts, maintenance and the duration of the required service belong in that comparison alongside the purchase price.']
